steps for installing python:

1.install the python using the dnf list , dnf install , dnf module list python
2.check for the python version
3.create /app
4.create the system variable to run the applicable since we need to have 1 system variable
useradd --system --home /app --shell /sbin/nologin --comments "comments" roboshop
5.download the package using the curl 
curl -o /tmp/roboshop.zip http://github.jkdjdjj/roboshop.zip
6.go to app folder and unzip there
cd /app
unzip /tmp/roboshop.zip
7./app should able to see the code base
8.now create the virtual environment and then we need to use the pip install there
python3.14 -m venv /app/.venv
9.once the .venv is created go to the bin and then use the pip install 
/app/.venv/bin/pip install -r requirment.txt
10.the package will be seen with in the /.venv 
11.go to the /etc/systemd/system and the create the service file
12.in the service file give the backend connection
13.reload the systemd ---> systemctl daemon-reload
14.systemctl restart servicename
15.systemctl enable servicename
16.systemctl start servicename
17.check the status of the servicesname
18.check health http:localhost:8080/health , netstat -lntp , telnet domainname 8080 , ps -ef | grep servicename ,logs if needed 